<body>
    <div class="container">
        <header>
            <h1><i class="fas fa-orbit"></i> Orbital Velocity Sandbox</h1>
            <p class="subtitle">Explore how changes in tangential velocity affect a planet's orbital path. Reduce velocity below the stable circular speed to observe orbital decay.</p>
        </header>

        <div class="content">
            <div class="card">
                <h2 class="card-title"><i class="fas fa-info-circle"></i> Orbital Mechanics</h2>
                <p>In celestial mechanics, a stable circular orbit occurs when the gravitational force provides exactly the centripetal force required for circular motion.</p>

                <div class="formula-card">
                    <div class="formula">
                        F<sub>gravity</sub> = F<sub>centripetal</sub>
                    </div>
                    <div class="formula">
                        G\frac{Mm}{r^2} = m\frac{v^2}{r}
                    </div>
                    <div class="formula">
                        v = \sqrt{\frac{GM}{r}}
                    </div>
                    <p class="formula-label">Stable Circular Velocity Formula</p>
                </div>

                <p>When a planet's tangential velocity is reduced below this critical value:</p>
                <ul style="padding-left: 20px; margin: 15px 0;">
                    <li>The gravitational force exceeds the required centripetal force</li>
                    <li>The planet begins to spiral inward</li>
                    <li>The orbit becomes elliptical with decreasing periapsis</li>
                    <li>If velocity is too low, the planet will collide with the star</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="card">
                <h2 class="card-title"><i class="fas fa-star"></i> Key Concepts</h2>
                <div class="info-panel">
                    <div class="info-box">
                        <h3>Stable Circular Orbit</h3>
                        <p>Occurs when tangential velocity exactly matches the orbital velocity required for a circular path.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="info-box">
                        <h3>Orbital Decay</h3>
                        <p>When velocity is too low, the orbit decays and the planet spirals inward due to excess gravitational pull.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="info-box">
                        <h3>Escape Velocity</h3>
                        <p>The minimum velocity needed to escape the gravitational influence: v<sub>escape</sub> = √(2GM/r)</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="info-box">
                        <h3>Elliptical Orbits</h3>
                        <p>At velocities between circular and escape velocity, orbits become elliptical.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div style="margin-top: 20px; background: rgba(0, 50, 80, 0.4); padding: 15px; border-radius: 10px;">
                    <h3><i class="fas fa-lightbulb"></i> Try This Experiment</h3>
                    <p>1. Set the velocity to 100% for a stable circular orbit</p>
                    <p>2. Gradually reduce velocity below 100%</p>
                    <p>3. Observe how the orbit becomes elliptical and eventually decays</p>
                    <p>4. Reset and try increasing above 100% to create elliptical orbits</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="simulation-container">
            <h2 class="card-title"><i class="fas fa-satellite"></i> Orbital Simulation</h2>
            <div class="canvas-container">
                <canvas id="orbitCanvas" width="800" height="500"></canvas>
            </div>

            <div class="controls">
                <div class="control-group">
                    <label class="control-label">Tangential Velocity (% of stable orbit)</label>
                    <div class="slider-container">
                        <input type="range" id="velocitySlider" min="20" max="180" value="100">
                        <span id="velocityValue" class="value-display">100%</span>
